          %p
            It turns out that the shifted flux quantization condition on the C-field is naturally implied (
            %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS1 19b, Prop. 4.12
            ) by the requirement that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
            is the differential form datum underlying, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            in unstable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
            in degree 4 (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"}> Hypothesis H
            ).
          %h2#ForElectricG7Flux
            For the electric
            = succeed "-flux" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7
          %p
            In the presence of non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-branes"} M2-branes
            is not
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo ⋆
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7 \coloneqq \star G_4
            alone, but receives corrections, first due to the quadratic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            self-interaction in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D11+supergravity"} D=11 supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            expected in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
              literature
            states the corrected 7-flux to be the following combination, also known as the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Page+charge"} Page charge
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "M2-brane#Page83"} Page 1983 (8)
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "M2-brane#DuffStelle91"} Duff &amp; Stelle 1991, (43)
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "M2-brane#BaggerLambertMukhiPapageorgakis13"} BLMP 13, p. 21
          #eq:FirstCorrectionToG7.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo ˜
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 7
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 4
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widetilde G'_7
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  G_7 + \tfrac{1}{2} C_3 \wedge G_4
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the second term subtracts the electric flux induced by the self-intersection of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+differential+form"} closed differential form
            if the naive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            hold:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ˜
                    %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d \widetilde G_7
                  \\;=\;
                  0
                  \\,.
          %p
            But in fact
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FirstCorrectionToG7"} (2)
            does not quite make general sense, for two reasons:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                In general
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4 = 0
                is not an admissible condition and is not the actual vanshing of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            %li
              %p
                Even if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
                happens to be intregrally quantizaed (if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 4
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{4}p_1
                is integral) the appearance of a globally defined
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
                potential
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_3
                in
                = succeed ",means" do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:FirstCorrectionToG7"} (2)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux"} flux
                actually does vanish after all.
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            %strong
              Charge-quantized
              = succeed "-flux" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi G
                          %mo ˜
                        %mn 7
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde G_7
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
            (
            %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS 19b, Prop. 4.3
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#FSS19c"} FSS 19c, Section 4
          %p
            Both of these issues are solved if the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
            is taken to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge+quantization"} charge quantized
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"}> Hypothesis H
            ). This gives the corrected formula
          #eq:FullCorrectionToG7.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ˜
                    %mn 7
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 7
                  %mo +
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi G
                      %mo ˜
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widetilde G_7
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  h^\ast G_7 + \tfrac{1}{2} H_3 \wedge h^\ast \widetilde G_4
          %p where
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %a{:href => ""}
              %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/6dWZFromHomotopyLifting.jpg", :width => "440"}/
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the expression lives on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
                of the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%282%29"} Sp(2)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parametrized+homotopy+theory"} parametrized
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mi ℍ
                      %mo ⫽
                      %mi Sp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      h \coloneqq h_{\mathbb{H}}\sslash Sp(2)
              %p
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
                that represents the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field"} C-field
                under
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hypothesis+H"} Hypothesis H
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi G
                          %mo ˜
                        %mn 4
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo +
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 4
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde G_4 \coloneqq h^\ast G_4 + \tfrac{1}{4}h^\ast p_1(\nabla)
                is the integral
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field
                pulled back to that 3-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibration"} spherical fibration
                over spacetime;
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo −
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 4
                      %msup
                        %mi h
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∇
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d H_3 = h^\ast G_4 - \tfrac{1}{4}h^\ast p_1(\nabla)
                trivializes not the C-field itself, but its pullback, and not absolutely but relative to the background charge implied by
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shifted+C-field+flux+quantization"} shifted C-field flux quantization
          %p
            With the corrected 7-flux in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+Cohomotopy"} twisted Cohomotopy
            it becomes true that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the integral of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 7
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7
                around the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
                linking a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
                is always
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
                (
                %a{:href => "#FSS19c"}> FSS 19c, Theorem 4.6
                );
            %li
              %p
                this integer satisfies the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field+tadpole+cancellation+condition"} C-field tadpole cancellation condition
                (
                %a{:href => "#FSS19b"}> FSS 19b, Section 4.6
                ).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-field+tadpole+cancellation"} C-field tadpole cancellation
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p The suggestion originates in
          %ul
            %li#Witten96a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On Flux Quantization In M-Theory And The Effective Action
                %strong 22
                1 (1997) 1-13 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9609122"}> arXiv:hep-th/9609122
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0393-0440(96)00042-3"} doi:10.1016/S0393-0440(96)00042-3
            %li#Witten96b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Five-Brane Effective Action In M-Theory
                %strong 22
                2 (1997) 103-133 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9610234"}> arXiv:hep-th/9610234
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0393-0440(97)80160-X"} doi:10.1016/S0393-0440(97)80160-X
          %p
            Proposals to model the condition by a
            = succeed "-shifted" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wu+class"} Wu class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            include
          %ul
            %li#HopkinsSinger02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"}> Michael Hopkins
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quadratic+Functions+in+Geometry%2C+Topology%2C+and+M-Theory"} Quadratic Functions in Geometry, Topology, and M-Theory
                J. Differential Geom. Volume 70, Number 3 (2005), 329-452. (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0211216"}> arXiv:math.AT/0211216
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1143642908"} euclid:1143642908
            %li#DiaconescuFreedMoore03
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duiliu-Emanuel+Diaconescu"}> Duiliu-Emanuel Diaconescu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"} Dan Freed
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The
                    = succeed "-theory" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi M
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
                    = succeed "-gauge" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi E
                              %mn 8
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haynes+Miller"} Haynes Miller
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Douglas+Ravenel"} Douglas Ravenel
                (eds.)
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elliptic Cohomology Geometry, Applications, and Higher Chromatic Analogues
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0312069"} arXiv:hep-th/0312069
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511721489"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511721489
            %li#FreedMoore04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Setting the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+integrand"} quantum integrand
                    of M-theory
                %strong 263
                1 (2006) 89-132 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0409135"}> arXiv:hep-th/0409135
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-005-1482-7"} doi:10.1007/s00220-005-1482-7
            %li#Moore04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"}> Greg Moore
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Anomalies, Gauss laws, and Page charges in M-theory
                %strong 6
                (2005) 251-259 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0409158"}> arXiv:hep-th/0409158
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.crhy.2004.12.005"} doi:10.1016/j.crhy.2004.12.005
            %li#FSS12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+moduli+3-stack+of+the+C-field"} The moduli 3-stack of the C-field
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1202.2455"} arXiv:1202.2455
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://link.springer.com/article/10.1007%2Fs00220-014-2228-1"} doi:10.1007/s00220-014-2228-1
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+W.+Moore"}> Gregory W. Moore
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vivek+Saxena"} Vivek Saxena
              = succeed "," do
                %em The M-Theory Abelian Gauge Field
              = succeed "," do
                %em TASI Lectures On Topological Field Theories And Differential Cohomology
              %a{:href => "https://sites.google.com/colorado.edu/tasi-2023-wiki/home"} TASI 2023
              lecture notes &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.07408"}> arXiv:2510.07408
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Suggestion that an actual
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"} E8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            on 11d spacetime plays a role here:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                D. Diaconescu,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                    Gauge Theory, and a Derivation of K-Theory from M-Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0005090"} arXiv:hep-th/0005090
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#DiaconescuFreedMoore03"} Diaconescu-Freed-Moore 03, Section 3
            %li
              %p
                Allan Adams,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jarah+Evslin"} Jarah Evslin
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The loop group of
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn 8
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_8
                    and K-theory from 11d
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0203218"} arXiv:hep-th/0203218
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"}> Hisham Sati
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
